{
  "summary": "The previous proposal correctly identifies the missing ActiveSlugs in the initial page render as a root cause, but has three weaknesses: (1) It claims the template 'crashes while rendering the first feature card in the ideas stage' — but the crash only occurs when there are actual features with cards to render. If ideas has no items, the template would proceed past it to the next stage with items, meaning the crash point depends on data, not on 'ideas' being first. The symptom 'only shows ideas' would only hold if ideas is the first stage WITH items. (2) More critically, the proposal underestimates the severity of the partial-render corruption — since html/template streams directly to the ResponseWriter, a mid-render crash produces malformed HTML (unclosed divs, broken attributes). This malformed DOM could break the JavaScript polling/replacement logic (the replaceChildren call at the board-container level), meaning the 5-second self-heal via /api/board may NOT work reliably since the JS that triggers it may itself be in a broken state depending on where the template aborted. The fix should also consider wrapping the initial template execution in a bytes.Buffer to prevent partial writes on error. (3) The secondary observation about collapsed empty stages is a separate UX issue, not the reported bug — conflating it muddies the diagnosis and could lead to the wrong fix being applied if someone addresses only the collapse behavior without fixing the nil ActiveSlugs map."
}
